return [
    'title' => 'Privacy Policy',

    's1_heading' => '1. Who we are',
    's1_body'    => 'KlassApp is an open education protocol for humans and agents. Schools run their records, marks, fees and parent messages through it, and parents receive their children\'s school updates on WhatsApp. KlassApp is operated by <strong>[legal entity name]</strong>, <strong>[registered address]</strong>, registration number <strong>[number]</strong> ("KlassApp", "we", "us").<br><br>This policy explains what personal information KlassApp handles, why, who we share it with, how long we keep it and the rights you have. It applies to our website klassapp.xyz, the KlassApp application and our WhatsApp services.',

    's2_heading' => '2. Schools and KlassApp: who is responsible',
    's2_body'    => 'Most information in KlassApp belongs to the school that uses it. For information about pupils, parents, guardians and staff that a school enters or collects through KlassApp, the school is the data controller and decides why and how the information is used. KlassApp processes that information on the school\'s behalf, only to provide the service, under a data processing agreement with each school.<br><br>KlassApp is the data controller for a small set of information about our own customers and visitors: school administrator accounts created at sign-up, demo and contact requests, people who contact us without an account, billing records and basic website usage.<br><br>If you are a parent, pupil or staff member and have a question about your information, you can contact your school directly or contact us (section 16) and we will help you reach the right person. Where a school is in another country, the data protection law of that country also applies to its records.',

    's3_heading' => '3. Information we handle',
