n applicants</td><td class="p-3 border align-top">The information in the school\'s public admission form, including the pupil\'s details, previous school and results, and parent or guardian contacts</td><td class="p-3 border align-top">To let the school process the application</td></tr><tr><td class="p-3 border align-top">Website visitors, demo and contact requests</td><td class="p-3 border align-top">Name, email, phone number, school, district and the message you send us</td><td class="p-3 border align-top">To reply to you and arrange a demo</td></tr><tr><td class="p-3 border align-top">People who contact us without an account</td><td class="p-3 border align-top">If you message our WhatsApp number or use a form without signing up: your phone number, WhatsApp display name, the messages you send, and the date and time</td><td class="p-3 border align-top">To reply to you, to keep a record of who has been in touch, and to follow up if you ask us to</td></tr><tr><td class="p-3 border align-top">Everyone who signs in</td><td class="p-3 border align-top">Sign-in, verification and reset codes (stored in hashed form and short-lived), IP address of sign-ins, and a record of important actions for security</td><td class="p-3 border align-top">To keep accounts secure and investigate misuse</td></tr></tbody></table>We do not ask for or keep national identification numbers of parents, parents\' income, ethnicity or tribe. We do not sell personal information, and we do not use pupils\' information for advertising. We do not use learners\' records for demonstrations, programmes or proofs of concept; demonstrations use made-up data only.',

    's4_heading' => '4. Children\'s information',
    's4_body'    => 'Most pupils are children. Schools are responsible for having a lawful basis for the pupil information they enter into KlassApp, including, where Uganda\'s Data Protection and Privacy Act 2019 requires it, the consent of a parent or guardian <strong>[lawyer to confirm the wording and the relevant sections]</strong>. KlassApp uses pupils\' information only to provide the service to their school.<br><br>Access to pupil information inside KlassApp depends on each user\'s role. For example, a bursar sees fee records and a class teacher sees their own class. Health and support notes are shown only to authorised staff and each view is recorded.',

    's5_heading' => '5. How we use information',
    's5_body'    => '<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1"><li>To provide KlassApp to schools: records, report cards, fees, attendance, admissions and messaging.</li><li>To send messages the school or the service needs to send, by WhatsApp and email, such as report cards, fee reminders, invitations and sign-in codes.</li><li>To keep KlassApp secure, prevent misuse and fix problems.</li><li>To support schools when they ask for help.</li><li>To reply to people who contact us and to keep a record of those contacts.</li><li>To improve KlassApp using information about how the service performs. We do not use pupils\' records to train artificial intelligence models.</li></ul>',

    's6_heading' => '6. WhatsApp, email and notifications',
    's6_body'    => '<strong>How parents join.</strong> KlassApp does not message anyone first. A parent links themselves to a child by messaging the KlassApp WhatsApp number or by completing the school\'s parent form, and the school approves the link. By linking, the parent agrees to receive messages from KlassApp on behalf of the school on WhatsApp: results, report cards, fee reminders and school notices.<br><br><strong>What we send.</strong> Once a parent is linked, the messages are the ones the school sends through KlassApp: exam results, report cards, fee reminders and school notices, plus replies when the parent writes to us. We do not send advertising or marketing, and we do not pass a parent\'s number to anyone to market to them.<br><br><strong>How to stop.</strong> A parent can reply STOP at any time to stop WhatsApp messages, and OPTIN to start again. A parent can also ask the school or us to remove a link.<br><br><strong>How messages are sent.</strong> KlassApp sends messages through the WhatsApp Business Platform operated by Meta. When a school sends a report card or message, the parent\'s phone number and the message content pass through Meta\'s service. Report card files shared by WhatsApp are made available through a secure link that expires, and the files are deleted from our temporary storage within 2 hours.<br><br>Emails such as sign-in codes, invitations and alerts are sent through our email delivery provider. Push notifications on mobile devices are delivered through Google Firebase.',

    's7_heading' => '7. Toshi, our AI assistant',
